# CSS (strict)

Plain global CSS in `src/styles/` only. **No** CSS modules, Tailwind, Sass, CSS-in-JS, or stylesheets next to components.

## Files

| File | Owns |
|------|------|
| `tokens.css` | `:root` and dark `[data-theme]` / `prefers-color-scheme` variables only |
| `shell.css` | app chrome: topbar, sidebar, workspace, buttons, empty/error |
| `views.css` | feature layouts (step, snapshot, evolution, map, welcome, settings) |
| `diff.css` | diffs, file viewer, syntax token classes |

Put a new class in the file that already styles that surface. Do not add a fifth stylesheet.

## Tokens

Every color, radius, font, and control height comes from `tokens.css` (`--bg`, `--text`, `--text-dim`, `--border`, `--accent`, `--add`, `--del`, `--radius-sm`, `--mono`, `--hl-*`, …).

```css
/* ❌ */
.color: #3d6be6;
background: white;

/* ✅ */
.color: var(--accent);
background: var(--bg-panel);
```

Hex (and raw rgba) belong **only** in `tokens.css`.

## Shape

- Class names: short **kebab-case**, existing vocabulary (`btn`, `btn-primary`, `btn-ghost`, `empty-state`, `repo-chip`). No BEM (`Block__Elem--mod`), no hashed names, no `css-` prefixes.
- Group with the house banner, then a blank line:

```css
/* -- top bar ---------------------------------------------------------------- */

.topbar {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 10px;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  background: var(--bg-panel);
}
```

- Reuse `.btn` / `.btn-primary` / `.btn-ghost` instead of restyling `<button>` per feature.
- No `!important`. No element restyles outside `tokens.css` resets. Delete unused selectors in the same change that removes the markup.
